WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.600
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.930
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.140
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:20.670
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:30.920
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.350
Go! Go!

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:37.730
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.630
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.000
Always in the good days in my life!

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:51.000
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:55.380
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.820
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.950
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.790
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.160
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.560
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:21.470
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.730
<i>Now make big circles with your arms!</i>

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.640
<i>One! Two! Three! Four!</i>

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.070
<i>Stretch your legs out wide!</i>

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.030
<i>One! Two! Three! Four!</i>

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.290
<i>Now like you're pushing against the ground!</i>

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.360
<i>One! Two! Three! Four!</i>

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.240
<i>And finally, take a deep breath!</i>

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:57.340
<i>One! Two! Three! Four! Five! Six! Seven! Eight!</i>

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.120
<i>Oh, that feels good!</i>

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.990
All right! I'm gonna give today my best!

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.350
Okay, bring it up! That's got it!

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:19.650
Hey, May! You're coming to the fireworks festival tonight, right?

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.680
Yeah, I'm coming.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.830
You'd like that, right, big brother?

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.250
Wh-Whaddaya mean? I just...

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.420
Masato, let's meet at the fireworks festival.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.210
R-Right...

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.960
Okay, let's all give this day our best!

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.170
YEAH!

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.270
Uh, May?

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:50.500
Sorry, Kazuya. I did it again!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.930
Looks like you're still not used to being big.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.480
Good morning.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.950
G-Good morning.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.320
Whoops...

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:06.580
I'm late because I was calculating the recipe for miso soup.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.130
Oh, I see...

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.750
There we go. Yo, guys!

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.880
Yo, guys!

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.020
Ikariya! Yo!

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.600
Oh, good morning, everyone.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.680
Morning!

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.840
Let's eat!

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.870
Chew it well!

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.530
I know, Ikariya!

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.070
Kazuya, the fireworks festival will be lots of fun, won't it?

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:44.370
The weather's perfect for it! I'm so excited!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:48.660
Yeah. I was worried yesterday because of all the rain,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.960
but I guess those good weather charms you made really worked.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.130
Oh, May, could you pass the soy sauce, please.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.750
Doing my best! Here you go, Kazuya!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.630
Analyzing the current temperature, humidity, barometric pressure,

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.880
and the wind's force, speed, and direction,

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.760
cross referenced with the weather data for the past 20 years,

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.680
the chances of rain tonight within a 3 km radius

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.020
of the Momiji river basin is 8.25%.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.420
Oh! Sunny-side up eggs taste best with salt!

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.270
I like them with sauce, actually.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.900
I like them with mayonnaise!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.360
How about tempura?

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.940
Kazuya likes it with soy sauce.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.320
Salt!

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.070
Sauce!

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.360
Mustard and mayonnaise!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.740
I like tempura sauce.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.310
I'll get you some more!

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.710
You know, I never really noticed when she was little,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:42.630
but May's pretty hot, isn't she, Kazuya?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.430
R-Really?

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.140
Lucky for you, Kazuya.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:46.970
What is?!

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:47.520
The weather.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:51.930
You've been looking forward to the fireworks festival, haven't you?

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.500
Yeah.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.770
Kei, I'm going out, too. Why don't we go together?

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:02.280
Sure thing. Just give me 3 minutes, 22.12 seconds, please.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.400
Are you going somewhere, Kei?

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.620
Yeah. She's starting a part-time job today as a lab assistant at my university.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.200
Here, Kazuya.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.640
Thank you, May. Oh, Kei? It's your first day there.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.620
You sure you don't need me to show you around?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.460
Are you that worried about me?

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:26.130
Uh, well, to make sure nobody finds out that you're a cyber doll.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:33.790
And Dr. Hell, who runs the class next door to Prof. Yumi, always sends chain e-mails to Yumi's new assistants...

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.330
s-so I've got a bad feeling about this...

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.400
Fireworks festival, huh?

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:48.640
Nanbara here. Oh, Sara? I've been waiting for your call!

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.080
No, make it a little more subdued.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.270
Ah, right on schedule.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.900
Not bad, but can I have something more original?

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.770
I'll get going as soon as I'm ready, so wait there for me.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.390
How can I go to the festival if I'm not flashier than the fireworks?!

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:03.670
So, there's no ramen there! Don't move! Got that?!

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.590
Who da hell do ya think ya are?!

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.500
Hello? Raku-Raku restaurant?

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.220
An order of miso ramen and ramen with pork slices, please.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.720
Deliver it to the roof of Kasumi House, please, and hurry!

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:29.080
May, is there anything good on sale today?

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.480
Yeah! I'll go shopping right now!

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.750
Kasumi, what do you want for lunch?

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.000
Sorry, gotta bail today.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.640
Got some stuff that I have to take care of.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:48.920
I gotcha. Okay, I'll pick something up for you, then.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.680
THANK YOU! Umm, I'll have...

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.890
...two melon rolls, right?

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.930
Sara! Where'd Saotome and the others go?!

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.420
Dunno...

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.810
"Dunno"?!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:01.150
Didn't you say that Cyber-whatsit company of yours ordered you to keep an eye on Saotome?!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.980
And you told me not to move.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.030
Geez, you're sure taking this assignment easy!

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.700
Is this important to your company or not?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.780
It seems to be a very serious matter, actually.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.580
Why do I get the feeling she doesn't care about this much?

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.710
No matter! Anyway, let's get to the fireworks festival early, Sara!

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.250
'Scuse me.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.630
What?

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.590
Nanbara, sir. What's with the outfit?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.590
A happy coat's the thing to wear for fireworks!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:32.430
This way, I'll be able to blend into the crowd!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.600
Don't worry, Sara. I brought one for you, too!

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:38.110
Yeesh... Seriously?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:45.100
Please! Ikariya counts as a person, too!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:48.330
It's okay, May. You don't have to do this for me.

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:51.610
Oh, Ikariya! You poor thing!

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:55.410
You're crying for me? Thank you, Rena!

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.080
Please?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.000
But...

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.240
Ikariya is a person, too!

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.000
Oh, just let them buy it!

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.790
Yeah. It's not like you're letting them have it for free.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.290
Please?

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.340
Ikariya!

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.420
That reminds me. I wonder if Kei's all right.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.610
Who left this banana peel on the floor?!

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.810
Shut up! Was it you?! Did you throw it on the floor?!

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.020
No, sir!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.410
Then who did it?!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.600
Oh, my aching butt!

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.060
Are you all right, sir?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.490
Ready, Kei?

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:38.870
Ready. Go ahead.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.000
Yo, guys!

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:51.050
Kazuya, what are May and Kei up to?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.670
Data transfer.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:58.600
They said cyber dolls can exchange data by touching hands.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.430
For instance, Kei asked May to transfer data on today's episode

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:05.640
of that afternoon soap opera, "The Whirlwind of Love."

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.440
Wow. That's really convenient.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.650
Yeah. Incredible, huh?

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.450
Um, Kasumi?

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.450
Did it come through?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.450
Kasumi...

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.460
What I was thinking about.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.360
Paying the rent?

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.800
Correct answer!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.010
Now, either pay up or get out!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:45.480
Kasumi! I'm sorry! I really am!

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.440
I'll pay you this week, I SWEAR!

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.440
Shikishima?

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.360
Wow...

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.040
K-Kasumi! I swear, I'll get you the rent, so...!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.910
What are you saying?

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:10.710
Well?

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:14.710
Those yukata... Oh! That's what Kasumi was carrying before!

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.590
Well, my mom did most of it.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:23.100
I figured if we're going to see fireworks, we should dress right for it.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:28.230
You all look really great in them. So, what do I wear?

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.740
Huh? Uh, that is...

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:34.930
Okay, let's go to the fireworks! Go! Go!

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:35.650
Go!

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.670
Uh, guys? Hold on here!

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:54.110
Let's get something to eat from the stands before the fireworks start.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:54.990
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:57.770
Those weather charms worked.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:00.900
Oh, you brought them.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.760
Yeah. I figured I'd take them to see the fireworks,

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.560
in return for their making sure the weather was nice.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.810
Oh, they're so cute! Weather charm dolls!

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.220
It's May!

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.530
Good evening!

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:15.870
Good evening.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:19.600
Now, Masato, you take care of Miyuki, okay?

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.450
Huh? Aw, Coach...

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.650
Coach! Coach!

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:26.690
Now, c'mon. When we're not playing baseball, greet me normally.

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:29.250
Okay. Yo!

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.090
Yo!

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:35.850
Wow...

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:36.590
What?!

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:40.760
Seeing you like this makes you look really cute, Rena.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:42.930
You just noticed?!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.080
I thought May was the only girl you were interested in.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:51.020
Well, May has so many fans that the competition's pretty stiff.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.300
What does that make me, the booby-prize?!

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.890
C'mon, Kazuya! Let's go!

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.010
Huh?! What? Hey!

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:00.220
Wait a second!

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.440
Oh, wait for us!

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:04.000
Wait!

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.780
Wait...

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.380
Wrist angle and water entry angle are set. All that's left is...

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:23.470
Cool! Cool! That was great!

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.260
We've got a lot of time till the fireworks start.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:27.270
Where to next? Huh?
We've got a lot of time till the fireworks start.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:29.720
Where to next? Huh?

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:31.500
Kazuya!

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.540
Hey! Quit shoving!

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:37.230
Ikariya, do you see Kazuya?

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:37.240
It's no use!
Ikariya, do you see Kazuya?

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.360
It's no use!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.230
Big brother!

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:39.900
Miyuki!

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:40.820
Big brother!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:41.740
Miyuki!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.320
Huh? Guys? Kei, what do we do now?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.790
Huh? Kei? Oh, for Pete's sake...

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:55.290
Um, Master Nanbara? We're drawing attention here.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.920
What are you talking about? They're all just jealous!

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.380
Oh, really?

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.050
Never mind that. Where's Saotome and the others?!

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.130
Uh-oh...

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.950
You... little... brats...

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:12.180
You did that knowing I am the great Nanbara?!

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.680
I-It wasn't on purpose!

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:18.170
Come back here!

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:23.180
Uh, what about Saotome? Oh, never mind.

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:26.950
No soup... Wavy noodles... And they're grilled dark!

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.030
Can it be a new kind of ramen?!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:44.750
What was the name of the girl with glasses?

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:45.810
You mean Kei?

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:47.430
Yeah! Yeah! Kei!

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.180
May's good and all, but Kei's really pretty, too!

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.640
What's that mean?! That my Rena comes in third?!

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.130
That's not what I meant!

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.060
Then what <i>did</i> you mean?!

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.980
Where do I place in this contest?

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.320
Well, you're fourth...

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:06.150
Next up is first baseman Coach Kasumi, number 33!

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:08.270
Oh, Kazuya. Find them?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.980
No luck. I'll look over there now. You guys, stay here.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.290
Hey! Kazuya, I'll come, too!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.290
What bad little boys you are!

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.510
This stuff is great, too!

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.360
There's no way I'll find Kazuya Saotome in this crowd...

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:43.440
Where could May have gone?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.110
<i>Kazuya Saotome... found!</i>

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.840
Cool! I found 100 yen!

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:50.450
Look out!

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:55.880
Ow. Are you all right, Miss?

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:58.720
Huh? Sara?

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:01.830
Thank goodness.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:05.420
Sorry about that. Are you okay, Kazuya?

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:08.050
Just a scratch. Huh?

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.050
What?!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:16.060
Sara, are you a cyber doll, too?

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:21.060
Why, you little brats!

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.410
Will it get infected, Kazuya?

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.120
No, I'll just wash it like this,

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.460
and put a little saliva on it and I'll be fine.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.920
Good. Well, I'll bring Coach Kasumi and the others over here.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.630
You cure wounds with saliva?

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:51.010
Saliva protects you from infections.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.630
That's what my grandma says, anyway.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:56.470
The same way a computer uses a virus guard program.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.180
How does it work with cyber dolls?

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:04.230
We cyber dolls have a self-evolving virus guard installed.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:06.650
It gives us perfect protection. Also,

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:11.650
small wounds are instantly repaired by nanomachines in our bodies.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.950
You cyber dolls are incredible.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:19.700
S-So, you see, getting hurt helping a cyber doll

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.160
doesn't gain you anything.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.960
That doesn't matter to me.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.960
It doesn't matter if you're a human or a cyber doll when you help people.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:34.510
Anyway, sorry for all the trouble I caused you with May.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:37.600
If you want, you and Nanbara should stop by and visit sometime.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.100
U-Uh, s-sure.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:43.310
Anyway, I have to find a lost girl. If you'll excuse me...

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.100
U-Uh, wait...

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:48.610
It doesn't matter if you're human or a cyber doll, huh?

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:55.990
Humidity rising, barometric pressure changing.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.560
Wind direction remains constant...

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.030
Oh, Masato.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.670
Masato saved me.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.980
Aw, it was nothing.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:11.170
So, what about May and, more importantly, Miyuki?

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.020
Hurry up and find them!

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:19.510
Sara's run off somewhere. I can't find Saotome.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.260
Those kids managed to get away,

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.970
and now I have to help some stupid little girl go pee?!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:29.190
Well, it's just 'cuz I got separated from May and the others.

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:33.190
Don't cry! I Only want to see Saotome looking sad!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.150
I don't want to see little kids crying!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.870
Excuse me? Has anyone seen a little girl

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.490
wearing a yukata with chicks on it?

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:41.600
May!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:46.080
Miyuki! Thank goodness! I looked all over for you!

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:51.380
I was okay. That guy there was with me all the time.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:55.800
Oh, Kotaro Nanbara. Kazuya's best friend, schoolmate, and greatest enemy.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:59.260
None other! I'm Kazuya's best friend and greatest enemy!

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:02.060
Last name Nanbara, first name Kotaro...

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.060
You said Kazuya, like...!

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.060
Good evening.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.770
Dynamite! Oh, wow! Whatta babe!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.520
Oh, that glossy, lovely, cute brown hair of hers!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.360
Those sparkling eyes that look like diamonds!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.280
Those cute, lovely lips that seem to say "hello"!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.950
I... I'm in love!

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.240
Thank you very much, Nanbara.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:20.070
Thank you.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:25.830
Kazuya's waiting for us, so if you'll excuse me...

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.000
Let's go, Miyuki.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.830
Okay. Bye-bye!

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:31.920
Bye-bye...

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:32.790
Oh, May.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:33.920
Kazuya.

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.130
Big brother!

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.720
Miyuki! Where'd you run off to?!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.470
Hey, is that Masato?

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:41.300
His sister Miyuki's with him, too.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.390
And so is May!

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.390
May... Where have I heard that name before?

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.600
May? May? May... May!

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.160
I seem to recall when Sara reclaimed that thing.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.900
That means she's Saotome's mini-bot!

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:59.100
She's gotten huge! But, she's also a babe!

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:03.780
Oh, May. Leave Kazuya and come with me!

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:06.160
With my jokes, I'll navigate you to...

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.750
escort you to, give to you a garden of smiles!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:10.670
I'm so happy!

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.880
Come to me! Into my arms!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.880
Together, we shall see Saotome in a state of shock!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.840
Nanbara my love, you've already put me in a state of shock!

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:18.420
Oh, May...

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:29.480
<i>Due to the weather, the start of the fireworks is now on rain delay.</i>

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.600
I have to go to the bathroom.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:34.980
Kasumi? Kasumi?

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.490
Come on, weather charms!

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.160
Kazuya's been looking forward to these fireworks!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.330
Please stop the rain. Please try.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.260
I used to make those when I was little.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.710
Huh? You did, Kazuya?

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:55.090
Yeah. I'd ask them to make the skies clear.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.840
I'd wish as hard as I could while I made them.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:00.510
When I think about it, what I thought back then

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.560
was like my wish now of "If only I could do that..."

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:06.810
Kazuya...

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:14.060
And as I grew up, I learned how to do lots of things.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.100
Somehow, things have fallen into place.

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:18.900
I don't mind if it takes a while,

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.780
because I want to make something myself,

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:24.070
and hope that someday my dream can become something more.

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:25.340
You can do it!

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:27.780
You always give it everything you've got, Kazuya.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:28.710
I'm sure you can do it!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.280
Yeah.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:50.640
All right!

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:56.180
Oh, well. Okay, then!

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.610
Oh, Kasumi!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.230
Looks like the rain's stopped.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:00.960
Yeah.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:09.690
The fireworks have started, Master Nanbara.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.080
I know. My heart is already a skyrocket in flight.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:15.000
And soon the fireworks of my love for May

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.730
will launch over the Niagara Falls of love! May! J'et aime!

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:27.500
<i>The fireworks I saw with Kazuya were so pretty.</i>

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:31.480
<i>I may have only been 1/6 Kazuya's size till now,</i>

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:35.810
<i>but even these little weather charms could work when they tried their best.</i>

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:39.060
<i>Now that I'm big, I only have 1/6th of a chance at failing.</i>

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:41.840
<i>I'll keep my spirits high and try more and more</i>

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:44.320
<i>to do my best for Kazuya!</i>

00:21:53.010 --> 00:22:02.040
Kimi no mae de mimi made akaku naru no wa

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:06.310
Doushite darou

00:22:06.310 --> 00:22:12.520
Futari-kiri wa nigatedashi

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:19.690
Oshaberi mo gikochinai

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:27.500
Okashii yo ne ishiki shisugi

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:36.640
Kore ga koi na no? Sonna no zettai mitomenai

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:43.650
Sunao ni narenai sunao ni naritai

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:50.320
Hontou no kimochi wa kokoro no naka

00:22:50.320 --> 00:22:57.960
Itsuka kimi ga oshiete

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:01.730
Kei! Kei!

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:03.210
What's up, Rena?

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:05.240
Kasumi's really a guy?!

00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:06.030
Huh?

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:09.950
'Cuz she always says "Oissu!" Get it?
